pdf","committee":"Council Executive","date":"24/02/2026","key":true},{"title":"General Fund Revenue Budget 202627 and Council Tax Report","url":"https://moderngov.erewash.gov.uk/documents/s41652/general-fund-revenue-budget-202627-and-council-tax-report.pdf","committee":"Council Executive","date":"24/02/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Council Executive","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-19","committee":"Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-25","committee":"Council Executive","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-26","committee":"Borough and Parish Councils' Forum","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-08","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council Executive","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://Erewash.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"From 1 April 2027, the council will restrict permanent recruitment to essential posts only; senior management will shift to temporary or shared arrangements","lead":"Severe restrictions on recruitment and temporary management structures during final transition months create operational risk - reduced institutional knowledge, potential service continuity issues, and limited decision-making capacity at a critical time.","iso":"2026-07-22","paper_title":"1. 2027 Budget Strategy Report","paper_url":"https://erewash.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s42782/42782.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"From late 2026/early 2027, a Section 24 regime will require Shadow Council consent for major financial commitments above set thresholds","lead":"Section 24 restrictions could delay or prevent necessary financial or capital decisions during the critical transition period, reducing operational flexibility when it is most needed. Their imposition also signals government concern about financial\u2026","iso":"2026-07-22","paper_title":"1. 2027 Budget Strategy Report","paper_url":"https://erewash.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s42782/42782.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"The council will rely on drawing down the Financial Sustainability Reserve to cover projected budget deficits rather than making structural spending adjustments","lead":"Using reserves to fund ongoing deficits is unsustainable - it masks structural problems rather than solving them, potentially forcing abrupt decisions on the new unitary council immediately after vesting if the FSR is insufficient.","iso":"2026-07-22","paper_title":"1. 2027 Budget Strategy Report","paper_url":"https://erewash.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s42782/42782.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council Executive","paper_title":"1. 2027 Budget Strategy Report","paper_url":"https://erewash.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s42782/42782.pdf","headline":"From 1 April 2027, the council will restrict permanent recruitment to essential posts only; senior management will shift to temporary or shared arrangements","detail":"The council has committed to hiring permanent staff only where essential for service delivery or LGR support from April 2027 onwards. Senior management posts will transition to temporary arrangements or resource-sharing with other councils. This represents a material tightening of staffing discretion and capacity during the final nine months before vesting.","category":"people","matters":"Severe restrictions on recruitment and temporary management structures during final transition months create operational risk - reduced institutional knowledge, potential service continuity issues, and limited decision-making capacity at a critical time.","figures":"Staffing restrictions effective 1 April 2027 through vesting day 1 April 2028","quote":"From 1 April 2027, the Council expects to only undertake permanent recruitment to any vacant post where it is essential for the delivery of services. From 1 April 2027, for senior management posts \u2013 the Council expects to use temporary arrangements or, where possible, seek to share resources with other Councils.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council Executive","paper_title":"1. 2027 Budget Strategy Report","paper_url":"https://erewash.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s42782/42782.pdf","headline":"From late 2026/early 2027, a Section 24 regime will require Shadow Council consent for major financial commitments above set thresholds","detail":"The Structural Changes Order will trigger Section 24 directions requiring the Shadow Council's formal consent for decisions exceeding specified thresholds: land disposals over \u00a3100k, capital contracts over \u00a31m, and revenue contracts over \u00a3100k with impacts extending beyond vesting day. This creates a consent-based governance framework that will constrain the council's financial decision-making until 1 April 2028.","category":"governance","matters":"Section 24 restrictions could delay or prevent necessary financial or capital decisions during the critical transition period, reducing operational flexibility when it is most needed. Their imposition also signals government concern about financial stability risks.","figures":"Land disposals > \u00a3100,000; Capital contracts > \u00a31,000,000; Revenue contracts > \u00a3100,000 whole-life cost","quote":"Once the SCO is in place and the Section 24 Direction is issued certain decisions by predecessor councils will require the consent of the Shadow Council. Thresholds for consent commonly include: Land disposals > \u00a3100,000. Capital contracts > \u00a31,000,000. Revenue contracts > \u00a3100,000 (whole life cost), where they extend beyond vesting day.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council Executive","paper_title":"1. 2027 Budget Strategy Report","paper_url":"https://erewash.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s42782/42782.pdf","headline":"The council will rely on drawing down the Financial Sustainability Reserve to cover projected budget deficits rather than making structural spending adjustments","detail":"The council's reserve strategy explicitly commits to using the Financial Sustainability Reserve to cover the projected revenue gaps (\u00a30.831m in 2027/28 and \u00a31.531m in 2028/29). This approach treats the reserve as a temporary buffer for recurring structural imbalances rather than making cuts or finding permanent solutions to budget gaps. The FSR balance will consequently shrink from \u00a32.798m to \u00a31.446m.","category":"reserves","matters":"Using reserves to fund ongoing deficits is unsustainable - it masks structural problems rather than solving them, potentially forcing abrupt decisions on the new unitary council immediately after vesting if the FSR is insufficient.","figures":"FSR projected to cover \u00a30.831m (2027/28) and \u00a31.531m (2028/29) deficits","quote":"Fund projected gaps (\"deficits\") in the MTFP via the Financial Sustainability Reserve to balance the budget","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council Executive","paper_title":"1. 2027 Budget Strategy Report","paper_url":"https://erewash.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s42782/42782.pdf","headline":"Total usable reserves will decline from \u00a315.3m to \u00a34.6m by March 2028, a 70% reduction driven by committed spending","detail":"The council plans significant drawdowns of earmarked reserves over the next two years. The Erewash Investment Fund (both tranches totalling \u00a36.372m) will be fully deployed to complete committed projects. The \u00a32m LGR reserve will fund transition costs. Additional reserves for Local Plan, Digital Transformation, and other purposes will also be exhausted. The Financial Sustainability Reserve will decline from \u00a32.798m to \u00a31.446m.","category":"reserves","matters":"The incoming unitary council will inherit a heavily depleted reserve position with minimal flexibility to absorb unexpected pressures, service demands, or transition impacts - leaving it operationally and financially vulnerable.","figures":"Total usable reserves: \u00a315,316k (1 April 2026) \u2192 \u00a34,606k (31 March 2028); Erewash Investment Fund: \u00a36.372k \u2192 \u00a30; Financial Sustainability Reserve: \u00a32.798k \u2192 \u00a31.446k","quote":"The EIF is fully allocated with funds held in reserves until spent.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council Executive","paper_title":"1. 2027 Budget Strategy Report","paper_url":"https://erewash.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s42782/42782.pdf","headline":"Medium-term financial forecasts have deteriorated significantly, with budget gaps nearly doubling for 2027/28","detail":"The council's projected revenue gap for 2027/28 has increased from \u00a30.420m (reported when the 2026/27 budget was approved) to \u00a30.831m - nearly a 100% increase. The 2028/29 gap has also worsened from \u00a31.120m to \u00a31.531m. The council acknowledges this position reflects additional emerging pressures and is likely to change again as 2026/27 performance is monitored.","category":"overspend","matters":"Deteriorating budget forecasts indicate structural imbalances will be inherited by the new unitary council, potentially requiring immediate spending decisions or further reserve drawdowns immediately post-vesting.","figures":"2027/28 gap: \u00a30.420m \u2192 \u00a30.831m; 2028/29 gap: \u00a31.120m \u2192 \u00a31.531m","quote":"Members will note that the position has moved compared to that reported when the budget was approved as additional pressures are envisaged for 2027/28. This position will likely change again as budget performance for 2026/27 is monitored.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-28"},"name":"Erewash","findings_total":48,"news_drafts_total":3}}